How would you handle a scenario where your streaming application in Azure Databricks needs to process data from multiple sources with varying data arrival patterns?

"When I have multiple streaming sources in Azure Databricks, not all sources send data at the same speed. For example, Kafka events may arrive immediately, while files from ADLS may arrive 10–15 minutes late.
To handle this, I configure a separate watermark for each source based on how late its data can arrive. This helps Spark know how long it should wait for late records.
When I join or combine these streams, Spark uses the watermarks to manage state and clean up old data.
By default, Spark waits for the slowest stream to ensure no valid data is missed. If the business wants faster processing and can tolerate losing some very late records, I can change the watermark policy to process data sooner.
I also monitor the lag of each stream so that if one source starts falling behind, I can identify and fix the issue quickly."
